<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P assigns BB- rating to Argentina's samurai bond.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P assigns BB- rating to Argentina's samurai bond.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's Corp (S&amp;P) said on Tuesday that it had issued a BB- rating to Argentina's 50 billion yen five percent samurai bond due on December 20, 2002.</p>
<p>S&amp;P said in a statement that the rating reflected a broad national consensus in favour of macroeconomic stability brought on by the Convertibility Plan and, more fundamentally, the high social costs of last year's recession. Contributing factors were a continuing weakness of public finances and a high public external debt burden, it said.</p>
<p>The outlook for the rating was stable, it said.</p>
</text>
